---
title: Poundcake
source: direct-input
servings: 12
yield: 12 servings
cook time: 1 hour and 30 minutes
---

Cream Butter & Sugar: Start with @butter{2.5%sticks}(Salted), creaming it briefly before gradually adding @granulated sugar{3%cups}. Mix for about ~{4%minutes} until creamy. 

Add Eggs: Incorporate @eggs{6%large}(room temperature) one at a time, allowing each to fully mix in before adding the next. 

Add Flavorings: Mix in @vanilla extract{2%tsp} and @almond extract{1%tsp}. 

Add Dry Ingredients: Gradually add the flour mixture (which includes @salt{1/2%tsp} and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}) to avoid making a mess. 

Incorporate Sour Cream: Finally, fold in @sour cream{8%oz}(room temperature). Tracy stresses that adding the sour cream last makes a significant difference. 

Bake: Pour the batter into a prepared #pan{} and bake at 325°F for approximately ~{90%minutes} (noting that oven times may vary).